---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Start Here — Cassian Creed" description="New to Cassian Creed? Start with three sourced, victim-first case files — then follow the thread into the explainers behind them.">
  <section class="sh">
    <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Start Here</p>
    <h1>New here? Start with these.</h1>
    <p class="sh__lede">Three case files are the best way in — each sourced from the public record, each told victim-first. Read one, then follow the thread into the explainers behind it.</p>

    <div class="sh__grid">
      <a class="door" href="/post/the-murder-of-rachel-morin-how-her-killer-was-found/">
        <div>
          <span class="door__no">Nº 01</span>
          <h2 class="door__title">The Murder of Rachel Morin</h2>
          <p class="door__desc">How investigative genetic genealogy found a killer who sat in no DNA database — convicted, with an appeal now pending.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="door__go">Read the case →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="door" href="/post/what-happened-in-the-idaho-student-murders-the-bryan-kohberger-case-explained/">
        <div>
          <span class="door__no">Nº 02</span>
          <h2 class="door__title">The Idaho Student Murders</h2>
          <p class="door__desc">The Bryan Kohberger case, explained — four students, the knife-sheath DNA that broke it, and the 2025 guilty plea.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="door__go">Read the case →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="door" href="/post/the-murdaugh-murders-how-alex-murdaugh-was-convicted-and-why-he-now-faces-a-new-trial/">
        <div>
          <span class="door__no">Nº 03</span>
          <h2 class="door__title">The Murdaugh Murders</h2>
          <p class="door__desc">A conviction — and why South Carolina's most-watched case now faces a new trial.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="door__go">Read the case →</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="sh__next">
      <p>Then go deeper: <a href="/post/what-is-coercive-control-the-signs-examples-and-what-to-do/">What Is Coercive Control?</a> — the warning sign behind so many of these cases, and what to do about it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="books-promo wrap" aria-label="The Case Files Library — the book">
    <p class="evidence evidence--accent">The Case Files Library</p>
    <h2 class="books-promo__heading">The Trail — $1.99</h2>
    <div class="books-promo__shelf">
      <a class="books-promo__item" href="/the-trail/">
        <img src="/covers/the-trail.jpg" width="150" alt="Book cover of The Trail by Cassian Creed" />
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="books-promo__bundle">The complete, sourced case file for Rachel Morin — with an exclusive A.I. AL Case Analysis.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="https://cassiancreed.beehiiv.com/products/the-trail?utm_source=website&utm_medium=start_here&utm_campaign=the_trail" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Buy The Trail — $1.99 →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="subscribe wrap" id="subscribe">
    <p class="evidence evidence--accent">The free newsletter</p>
    <h2>Subscribe free &mdash; get <em>How to Read a Case Like the Court Does</em></h2>
    <p>A charge isn&rsquo;t a conviction. A theory isn&rsquo;t proof. Subscribe and we&rsquo;ll send you <em>How to Read a Case Like the Court Does</em> &mdash; a plain-language framework for weighing evidence instead of guessing, the real difference between proof and speculation, and what a verdict actually settles (and what it doesn&rsquo;t). No weekly blast; unsubscribe anytime.</p>
    <form action="https://cassiancreed.beehiiv.com/subscribe" method="get" aria-label="Subscribe to the free Cassian Creed newsletter">
      <input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@email.com" aria-label="Your email address" />
      <input type="hidden" name="utm_source" value="website" />
      <input type="hidden" name="utm_medium" value="start_here_cta" />
      <input type="hidden" name="utm_campaign" value="lm_case_how-to-read-a-case" />
